'' AN OS TABLE HOLDS ONLY THE ARRAY KEYS THAT ADD TO A TARGET (TK-003): 'copy_to' is the
'' target's, not an OS's, and says which keys an OS table takes.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.bob/cache
'' CLEAN: build/.bob
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/build-os => build/.bob/pkg
'' WRITE: build/.bob/pkg/tiko.toml :: [package]\nname = "osdemo"\n[target.app]\nmain = "src/main.tiko"\n[target.app.linux]\ncopy_to = ["bin"]\n
'' ARGS: metadata -target linux-x86_64 --manifest build/.bob/pkg
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0144
'' EXPECT-OUT: unknown key 'copy_to' in [target.app.linux]: an OS table holds sources, resources, libs, libpaths and options
